      {
        "id": 229902,
        "name": "der andere Jan",
        "username": "der_andere_Jan",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/der_andere_jan/{size}/1881_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-03-11T20:31:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Density Control is a Self-Control power, it’s only usable on yourself.  If it’s done with a doodad, a Technology power would be fine.  Otherwise I’d actually go with Cosmic Energy (“The primal energies of the universe are yours to command”).  And the effect would be a mass hinder.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Cosmic is a great idea indeed!<br>\nI have been playing around with a concept of macroscopic quantum state (very cliché: Scientist creates a machine that meddles with his precise positioning in space/time, let’s call it the Uncertainty Generator, and takes on crimefighting to field-test its capabilities as a practical schroedinger’s cat).<br>\nRigging the Inventions power into that idea seemed a bit of a long shot, but now I think a combination of Intangibility and Cosmic Energy Manipulation should do the trick nicely. Might even throw in a very limited Teleportation at d6 or so, to cover the spatial effects.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:04:46.214Z",
